WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.918
This slide asks you to strengthen a

00:00:01.932 --> 00:00:05.851
CHECK constraint The clinic does not allow

00:00:05.877 --> 00:00:08.759
negative standard prices but the current threshold

00:00:08.772 --> 00:00:13.008
is deliberately too weak Run the example

00:00:13.035 --> 00:00:15.653
first so you understand its current behavior

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.748
Then change the threshold from negative one

00:00:18.761 --> 00:00:20.537
hundred to zero and run it again

00:00:22.391 --> 00:00:24.956
After the correction the negative test value

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:29.713
should be rejected In this exercise rejection

00:00:29.727 --> 00:00:33.755
is success It means PostgreSQL is enforcing

00:00:33.782 --> 00:00:37.514
the business rule Pay attention to the

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.869
difference between fixing the data and fixing

00:00:39.895 --> 00:00:42.661
the rule We are changing the schema

00:00:42.687 --> 00:00:45.293
constraint so future invalid values are also

00:00:45.319 --> 00:00:47.714
protected not only correcting one row
